        518.58544921875,
        481.3797607421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A 3rd order Bézier curve can be evaluated by",
      "bbox": [
        88.19696044921875,
        491.6947937011719,
        286.72174072265625,
        500.49176025390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "F(s) = (1 −s)3P0 + 3(1 −s)2sP1 . . .",
      "bbox": [
        88.19696044921875,
        508.7530212402344,
        250.0023193359375,
        521.0987548828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "+ 3(1 −s)s2P2 + s3P3, s ∈[0, 1],",
      "bbox": [
        110.0389404296875,
        524.9320678710938,
        258.0415344238281,
        537.2777099609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(17)",
      "bbox": [
        500.8719482421875,
        526.9867553710938,
        518.58544921875,
        535.7837524414062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where [P0, . . . , P3] is the set of control points for the spline. This expression allows us to evaluate",
      "bbox": [
        88.19696044921875,
        546.0489501953125,
        518.76904296875,
        555.8099365234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the B and E splines represented by the control points Bc and Ec, and to stitch together the overall",
      "bbox": [
        88.19696044921875,
        558.0039672851562,
        518.6515502929688,
        568.3447265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "G2 continuous path x, which consists of straight line segments and spline segments.",
      "bbox": [
        88.19692993164062,
        570.0087890625,
        454.031494140625,
        578.8057861328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We extend this approach to compute the curvature of the entire path, in order to apply a rough",
      "bbox": [
        100.15192413330078,
        581.9637451171875,
        518.7903442382812,
        590.7607421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "kinematic mapping between curvature and velocity. This mapping allows us to reparameterize the",
      "bbox": [
        88.1969223022461,
        593.9187622070312,
        518.7703857421875,
        602.7157592773438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ﬂight path in terms of time. By picking an endpoint for the trajectory optimizer based on a constant",
      "bbox": [
        88.1969223022461,
        605.874755859375,
        518.7804565429688,
        614.6717529296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "time along the seed path, the duration of the optimized trajectory is somewhat regularized. This",
      "bbox": [
        88.1969223022461,
        617.8297729492188,
        518.7803344726562,
        626.6267700195312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "helps to prevent the solver from wasting computational resources planning too far into the future",
      "bbox": [
        88.1969223022461,
        629.7847900390625,
        518.79052734375,
        638.581787109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and allows us to provide a more feasible estimate of ﬁnal velocity to the solver. We compute the",
      "bbox": [
        88.1969223022461,
        641.73974609375,
        518.7705078125,
        650.5367431640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ﬁrst and second order derivatives of F with respect to s, F′, and F′′. Pulling out the individual",
      "bbox": [
        88.1969223022461,
